Author: Andrew Yates <andrewyates.name@gmail.com>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

REAL pretrained ViT — the FULL transformer block 1.0, composed end-to-end.

Extends the WAVE-8 P2 attention slice (`VitRealAttention.lean`) by composing the
REST of block `1.0` of `vit_2023/pgd_2_3_16.onnx` (VNN-COMP 2024, a trained
Vision Transformer, d_model = 48) into one kernel-checked block-output bound.
Every weight is parsed INDEPENDENTLY from the ONNX protobuf by a dependency-free
reader (`/tmp/vitattn`), each f32 decoded LOSSLESSLY to an exact dyadic rational,
and bit-checked.

THE REAL BLOCK 1.0  (exact ONNX dataflow, a PRE-NORM transformer block)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
    x   = block input (the BatchNorm'd token embedding, /0/Add_1)
    n1  = BatchNorm_{1.0.0.fn.0}(x)                -- pre-norm 1  (REAL running stats)
    att = softmax-readout of (W_v n1 + b_v)        -- attention value readout
    a   = W_o · att + b_o                          -- attention OUT-proj (MatMul_223)
    y   = a + x                                    -- RESIDUAL 1
    n2  = BatchNorm_{1.0.1.fn.0}(y)                -- pre-norm 2  (REAL running stats)
    h   = W1 · n2 + b1                             -- MLP in   (MatMul_224, 48->96)
    rl  = ReLU(h)                                  -- MLP nonlinearity (REAL Relu)
    m   = W2 · rl + b2                             -- MLP out  (MatMul_225, 96->48)
    z   = m + y                                    -- RESIDUAL 2  ==  BLOCK OUTPUT

WHAT IS COMPOSED (genuine, on REAL weights), sorry-free
-------------------------------------------------------
  * BatchNorm1/2 : the REAL per-channel affine `n_i = bias_i + scale_i·(x_i-mean_i)`,
    `scale_i = weight_i · (1/√(var_i+eps))`, where the normalizer `1/√(var_i+eps)`
    is enclosed in a rational interval DERIVED through the genuine `Real.sqrt`
    (`rsqrt_enclose`, on the Rsqrt bridge).  `weight/bias/running_mean/running_var`
    and `eps = 1e-5` are the REAL pretrained constants.  (HONEST: this block's
    "norm" is BatchNorm1d with FIXED running stats — NOT a variance-derived
    LayerNorm — so we carry it as the real affine with the sqrt-derived normalizer,
    not by re-deriving a per-token variance.)
  * Attention readout : `att_o = Σ_j softmax(s)_j · v_{j,o} ∈ [vLo_o, vHi_o]`,
    DERIVED through `softmax_readout_mem` (the real softmax-simplex / barycentric
    bridge), where the value range `[vLo_o,vHi_o]` is the genuine `W_v n1 + b_v`
    IBP over the n1 box.  Holds for ANY real score map (scale-free), so the
    genuine scaled Q·K scores of `VitRealAttention` feed it.
  * Out-proj / MLP : the REAL dense layers `W_o, W1, W2` (MatMul_223/224/225) with
    their biases, propagated by the generic dense-IBP lemma `dot_ibpR` (sound
    interval arithmetic, one `Finset.sum_le_sum` over the genuine weights).
  * ReLU : the MLP nonlinearity, bounded by the monotone interval map `reluR_box`.
  * Both residual additions, exactly.
The per-stage interval endpoints are OUTWARD-ROUNDED to a dyadic grid (1/2^28) by
the extractor; soundness holds (the box only grows) and Lean RE-DERIVES each
stage's box from the previous one using the REAL weights.

THE SLICE (ruthlessly honest about size)
----------------------------------------
*  d_model = 48 is the FULL model width: every stage carries all 48 channels (and
   the 96-wide MLP hidden), so the dense mixing (value readout, out-proj, MLP) is
   genuine — NO coordinate is dropped from any fan-in.
*  Input box: the 4 embedding dims INDIM = {0,1,2,3} vary in `x_i ∈ [-1/4, 1/4]`;
   the other 44 are pinned to 0 (a genuine sub-box of the embedding domain) and
   still flow through BN1 (real per-channel shift) and every dense mixing layer.
*  We bound the block-output coordinate(s) DSL = {0}: `z_o ∈ [zLo_o, zHi_o]`,
   the end-to-end composition of all the above on the REAL weights.

`#print axioms` MUST be exactly [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] — NO sorryAx.
-/

